
January Prayer Letter
January 15, 2014	· by narcolapser	· Bookmark the permalink. ·

Thus dawns 2014 and the beginning of my 5th month here.CIMG3349

The New Years outreach is done. All the extra people who joined us have departed for their homes all across the planet, and I feel exhausted. But the Lord blessed us in Dancelink with some great people and decent weather. While I feel tired and worn out, it is the kind of tiredness that comes with a sense of accomplishment from a job well done.

Many of the people who participated in the dance ministry part of the outreach had never danced before. They were excited and terrified, particularly when we went out and danced in the streets of Birmingham for the first time. But they rose to the challenge. We were so blessed and looking back I can see how everyone praying for us really helped. Thank you to all of you who prayed.

I have video recordings of the dances we did (many, many of them because everyone with a phone was recording), so I’ve picked some of the recordings to share with you here. One piece you may recognize as the piece we did for the Halloween outreach. The other dance, a hip hop piece, is a newer one. This dance is about freedom. The freedom to praise God in our sorrows. Freedom to praise God when we feel his majesty all around us. And it reminds us that we can change the world, just as God has changed us.

One of the highlights for me though was watching the extra volunteers, many of whom were high-school or college students, go talk to people and share the love of God with them. Many of the students were terrified with this first-time experience. Talking to a stranger can be very hard. Then add in the fact that English is not your first language, and it is a tall, tall mountain to try and get over. But I saw one girl amongst the group change after she did share for the first time. She talked and shared the Gospel with a chap from who was watching the drama she had just been a part of performing. She talked to me afterwards, more excited than I’d ever seen her. She found that English being a second language was not a problem, but rather a blessing. It made her slow down and think about the words. Had she been speaking in German (her mother tongue) she would have gone too fast and lost the person’s attention.

This is one of many examples of God’s ability to take our short comings, our flaws, our failures, and turn them into something wonderful for his glory.

Prayer requests:

Praise the Lord that there was not a big computer problem during the outreach. The other three who normally help me manage the computer systems here were gone on holiday leave, so I was the only left. If there had been a major computer crisis it would have been the worst timing possible because I was so involved with Dancelink and the outreach. I am so grateful that God kept watch over our network for me in the times I couldn’t be there.
Pray for those people to whom we talked to during the outreach and for the volunteers who helped us. Pray that those who heard will feel moved to find God’s love again or for the first time. And pray that the volunteers would feel God’s love for them after doing such good work.
Pray for rest for myself. The outreach has kept me busy through the last two weekends, so I’ve not had much time to simply rest.
Pray for the rest of my support. I’m still a little bit short of being fully financially supported and praying that the rest would come in soon.

God bless,

Toby

